WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.316 --> 00:00:06.618
Mazatl’s house was very simple.

2
00:00:06.638 --> 00:00:13.781
It was made adobe clay bricks.

3
00:00:13.941 --> 00:00:16.503
The house was one big room divided into separate areas.

4
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.681
Vinnie and Mandy met Mazatl’s mother.

5
00:00:33.702 --> 00:00:36.164
She was making flat pancake-like bread.

6
00:00:36.184 --> 00:00:41.727
“These corn tortillas are for your papa,” she said to Mazatl.

7
00:00:41.747 --> 00:00:45.069
“But please take a bath first.”

8
00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:49.352
Mazatl led them to another building.

9
00:00:49.372 --> 00:00:53.014
“This is our bath hut,” he explained.

10
00:00:54.215 --> 00:00:56.296
Vinnie and Mandy saw a mud hut.

11
00:00:57.488 --> 00:01:00.369
It had a chimney on the side with a hot fire.

12
00:01:00.389 --> 00:01:04.530
“The chimney heats the walls inside.

13
00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:06.851
We throw water on the walls.

14
00:01:07.891 --> 00:01:09.291
And we get lots of steam.

15
00:01:10.192 --> 00:01:15.033
We come here to get clean, but also when we are sick,” Mazatl explained.

16
00:01:15.053 --> 00:01:17.654
“Does it make you better?”

17
00:01:18.194 --> 00:01:18.994
asked Mandy.

18
00:01:19.014 --> 00:01:20.535
“Oh yes!”

19
00:01:21.155 --> 00:01:22.115
replied Mazatl.

20
00:01:22.135 --> 00:01:25.276
“I once had bad pains in my chest.

21
00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.261
The steam and heat made me well again.

22
00:01:29.341 --> 00:01:31.762
You go first,” he said to Mandy.

23
00:01:34.483 --> 00:01:36.283
Mandy had a quick steam bath.

24
00:01:37.383 --> 00:01:38.284
So did Vinnie.

25
00:01:39.224 --> 00:01:42.445
When they came out, Mazatl had fresh clothes for them.

26
00:01:43.225 --> 00:01:47.186
Vinnie got a short skirt and a cloak to wear over one shoulder.

27
00:01:48.027 --> 00:01:51.488
Mandy got a colorful sleeveless shirt and a skirt.

28
00:01:53.956 --> 00:01:57.477
“My mother and sister wove these clothes,” Mazatl said.

29
00:01:57.497 --> 00:01:59.538
“You can return them later.”

30
00:01:59.558 --> 00:02:04.999
“Thank you, they’re beautiful,” replied Mandy.

31
00:02:06.239 --> 00:02:08.740
Then Mazatl bathed and changed too.

32
00:02:12.661 --> 00:02:17.342
and his family are so nice,” Mandy whispered to her brother.

33
00:02:17.362 --> 00:02:22.624
“I can’t believe the Aztecs make human sacrifices.”

34
00:02:24.284 --> 00:02:26.245
Vinnie didn’t want to think about it.

35
00:02:28.325 --> 00:02:33.326
Taking the tortillas from his mother, Mazatl led Vinnie and Mandy to a canoe.

36
00:02:34.847 --> 00:02:36.747
They got to the crowded market.

37
00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:39.788
Vinnie and Mandy were amazed!

38
00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:46.010
People arrived in canoes or carried their goods on their backs.

39
00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:49.971
They could hear voices arguing loudly.

40
00:02:49.991 --> 00:02:55.112
“I need to find my papa,” said Mazatl.

41
00:02:55.132 --> 00:02:58.634
They walked past people selling many interesting things.

42
00:03:03.277 --> 00:03:04.618
those bear skins?”

43
00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:08.220
Mandy asked, pointing to a stack of fur.

44
00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:12.382
“Bears? Those are puma and jaguar skins.

45
00:03:13.263 --> 00:03:16.344
Only the rich can afford them,” Mazatl explained.

46
00:03:18.846 --> 00:03:22.268
Vinnie also noticed a man holding a bag of something.

47
00:03:23.596 --> 00:03:26.718
“I will give you three rabbits for those cocoa beans!”

48
00:03:27.718 --> 00:03:29.299
a buyer yelled at the man.

49
00:03:29.319 --> 00:03:34.602
“Give me five rabbits and two geese,” the seller shouted back.

50
00:03:34.622 --> 00:03:37.044
“Are you mad?

51
00:03:37.504 --> 00:03:39.365
I don’t have that many animals!”

52
00:03:40.245 --> 00:03:41.406
the buyer screamed.

53
00:03:41.426 --> 00:03:43.947
“I’m offering you a bargain!

54
00:03:44.208 --> 00:03:45.208
Take it or leave it!”

55
00:03:45.868 --> 00:03:47.069
the seller shouted.

56
00:03:47.089 --> 00:03:50.631
“Oh, no!”

57
00:03:51.211 --> 00:03:51.972
Mandy said.

58
00:03:53.128 --> 00:03:55.829
“I think those two men are going to fight.”

59
00:03:56.709 --> 00:04:00.950
Mazatl laughed and said, “Don’t worry.

60
00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:02.751
The judges are watching them.”

61
00:04:02.771 --> 00:04:05.672
“Judges?” asked Vinnie.

62
00:04:07.632 --> 00:04:09.873
Just then a tall man walked over.

63
00:04:11.013 --> 00:04:13.194
He said a few words to the buyer.

64
00:04:14.014 --> 00:04:15.855
The man nodded and walked away.

65
00:04:15.875 --> 00:04:20.476
“Our judges are wise and fair,” Mazatl said.

66
00:04:21.708 --> 00:04:23.770
“What exactly do the judges do?”

67
00:04:24.571 --> 00:04:25.251
asked Vinnie.

68
00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:28.895
Mazatl looked at his new friends strangely.

69
00:04:28.915 --> 00:04:32.098
“Judges make sure people behave fairly.

70
00:04:33.319 --> 00:04:34.840
We must obey what they say.

71
00:04:35.821 --> 00:04:36.982
Surely you know that.”
